# Files git does not track that a fresh worktree still needs in order to build or verify.
# `air worker` copies everything named here out of the main checkout and into the new
# worktree. gitignore syntax, one pattern per line; `!` negations are not supported.
#
# `private/` holds everything that names an adopter, and `private/adopters.md` is the list
# `air adopter-check` reads. Without this line a worker's worktree has no copy, the check has
# nothing to check, and `make verify` goes green over a leak (air-jsz).
private/
